<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lygdamis of Naxos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 540–524 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lygdamis was tyrant of the island of Naxos in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a> in the mid-6th century BCE. A Naxian aristocrat, he helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peisistratus">Peisistratus</a> regain power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and in return received his help in seizing Naxos around 540 BCE. He began ambitious building works, including the great temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> whose gateway, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portara">Portara</a>, still stands, and was overthrown by the Spartans around 524 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lygdamis-of-naxos.jpg" alt="Lygdamis of Naxos" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heiko Gorski (Moonshadow) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naxos_Gate.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
